# External Embedding

## Architecture

```
VITE_EMBED_ALLOWED_ORIGINS="https://wiki.example.com,https://grafana.internal.com"
              ↓
  shared/lib/embed.tsx → allowlist (+ auto: Jitsi, Workspace API)
              ↓
  isEmbedAllowed(url) → true/false
              ↓
  <EmbedFrame url={url} title="Wiki" sandbox="interactive" />
              ↓
  <iframe sandbox="allow-scripts allow-same-origin allow-forms allow-popups" />
```

## Usage

```tsx
import { EmbedFrame, isEmbedAllowed } from "~/shared/lib/embed";

// Check before rendering
if (isEmbedAllowed(url)) {
  <EmbedFrame
    url="https://wiki.example.com/page"
    title="Corporate Wiki"
    sandbox="interactive"     // "strict" | "interactive" | "full"
    className="h-[600px]"
    onLoad={() => log.info("loaded")}
    fallback={<p>Content blocked</p>}
  />
}
```

## Sandbox Levels

| Level | Permissions | Use case |
|-------|-----------|----------|
| `strict` | scripts, same-origin | Read-only dashboards, documentation |
| `interactive` | + forms, popups | Wiki, form-based tools |
| `full` | + downloads, popup-escape | Full-featured web apps (Grafana, etc.) |

## Security

- Only `https:` and `http:` protocols allowed
- Origin must be in `VITE_EMBED_ALLOWED_ORIGINS` (or auto-allowed: Jitsi, Workspace)
- `referrerPolicy="strict-origin-when-cross-origin"` on iframe
- Sandbox attribute always present (never unrestricted)
- Blocked URLs logged with `logger.warn`

## Auto-allowed Origins

- Jitsi Meet domain (from `VITE_JITSI_MEET_DOMAIN`)
- Workspace API origin (from `VITE_WORKSPACE_API_ORIGIN`)

These don't need to be listed in `VITE_EMBED_ALLOWED_ORIGINS`.

## For AI Agent

- Use `<EmbedFrame>` — never raw `<iframe>`
- Always check `isEmbedAllowed(url)` before rendering
- Choose minimum sandbox level needed
- New embedded services → add origin to `VITE_EMBED_ALLOWED_ORIGINS`
